onary\"\n// es5\nconst Dictionary = require(\"tonal-dictionary\")\n```\n**Example**  \n```js\nDictionary.chord(\"Maj7\") // => [\"1P\", \"3M\", \"5P\", \"7M\"]\n```\n\n* [Dictionary](#module_Dictionary)\n    * [`.scale(name)`](#module_Dictionary.scale) ⇒ <code>Array</code>\n    * [`.chord(type)`](#module_Dictionary.chord) ⇒ <code>Array</code>\n\n<a name=\"module_Dictionary.scale\"></a>\n\n## `Dictionary.scale(name)` ⇒ <code>Array</code>\nA dictionary of scales: a function that given a scale name (without tonic)\nreturns an array of intervals\n\n**Kind**: static method of [<code>Dictionary</code>](#module_Dictionary)  \n**Returns**: <code>Array</code> - intervals  \n\n| Param | Type |\n| --- | --- |\n| name | <code>string</code> | \n\n**Example**  \n```js\nimport { scale } from \"tonal-dictionary\"\nscale(\"major\") // => [\"1P\", \"2M\", ...]\nscale.names(); // => [\"major\", ...]\n```\n<a name=\"module_Dictionary.chord\"></a>\n\n## `Dictionary.chord(type)` ⇒ <code>Array</code>\nA dictionary of chords: a function that given a chord type\nreturns an array of intervals\n\n**Kind**: static method of [<code>Dictionary</code>](#module_Dictionary)  \n**Returns**: <code>Array</code> - intervals  \n\n| Param | Type |\n| --- | --- |\n| type | <code>string</code> | \n\n**Example**  \n```js\nimport { chord } from \"tonal-dictionary\"\nchord(\"Maj7\") // => [\"1P\", \"3M\", ...]\nchord.names(); // => [\"Maj3\", ...]\n```\n","maintainers":[{"name":"danigb","email":"danigb@gmail.com"}],"time":{"modified":"2022-06-27T18:17:11.542Z","created":"2016-05-08T08:55:46.388Z","0.50.0":"2016-05-08T08:55:46.388Z","0.60.0":"2016-11-15T15:07:44.561Z","0.61.0":"2016-11-16T00:43:52.980Z","0.67.0":"2016-11-22T00:24:26.682Z","0.68.0":"2016-11-28T00:57:36.417Z","0.68.1":"2017-01-31T09:25:38.451Z","0.69.0":"2017-02-16T23:04:29.561Z","0.69.1":"2017-03-14T15:26:38.384Z","0.69.2":"2017-04-04T20:50:20.071Z","0.69.3":"2017-04-04T21:10:01.651Z","0.69.4":"2017-04-04T21:48:59.872Z","0.69.5":"2017-04-04T22: